      "SourceContent": "# Original local-node admission observation proposal\r\n\r\nThis standalone source-only collector runs the immutable original admission probe and the same Erlang source used by the SDK compiled setnode contracts in two separate fresh unnamed OTP VMs. It uses the already validated raw-byte NodeProcess capture implementation, including timeout and inherited-pipe handling. Source-build evidence, installed-root OTP_VERSION, exact probe hashes, scenario inventories, actual runtime identity and fresh output are checked; a report records raw observations without SDK expected values or a semantic compatibility claim.\r\n\r\nThe copied original admission probe observes retained external creation4, argument errors, duplicate legacy node events and kernel death/reset. The compiled driver observes missing-kernel error, inactive/active state, map monitoring, minimum active creation, already-active failure and cleanup. Its fresh scenario intentionally has no retained epoch, matching the SDK compiled fixture's creation4 case. All ETF outcomes, outer exception and raw streams remain artifacts.\r\n\r\nNo native execution or collector build has occurred for this proposal. Promote the files to tools/Erlang.LocalNodeAdmissionContrasts and the workflow template to .github/workflows/local-node-admission-contrasts.yml only after source review and bounded collector validation. Publish first, then dispatch that workflow against the pinned original source. Compare actual outcomes after capture, including exact exception class/reason and local event shapes. Do not reinterpret capture completeness as semantic agreement. SDK custom function-factory barriers, CLR owner rejection, dictionary/hash stability and registry lock-order controls remain HOST-only evidence.\r\n"
